Project Map Skill for Claude
============================

This Claude skill maps your project structure, tracks changes,
and generates a persistent project map (`project.map.md`) for Claude to reference.

Supported project types:
- Split: Separate FE + BE projects (e.g. React + .NET API)
- Unified: Single project where UI + services coexist (e.g. Blazor Server, MVC, Razor Pages)

Features:
- Auto-categorizes files by layer (Pages/UI, Services, Domain, Infrastructure)
- Automatic updates on project changes (with cooldown)
- Persistent context to avoid rescanning
- Interactive setup asks for project type on first run

Folder Structure
----------------
project-root/
+-- .claude
|   +-- skills
|       +-- project_map
|           +-- project.map.md         <- auto-generated map file
|           +-- map.rules.md           <- Claude rules for referencing the map
|           +-- ai_map_updater.py      <- generates/updates the map
|           +-- map_watcher.py         <- watches project changes
|           +-- watcher_config.json    <- saved configuration (auto-created)

Prerequisites
-------------
- Python 3.10+ installed
- pip (Python package manager)

Installation Steps
------------------

1. Install Python
- Download Python: https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/
- Check "Add Python to PATH" during installation
- Verify installation:
  > python --version

2. Place Project Map Skill
- Copy the folder `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/project-map` into your project root.

3. Start the Watcher
- From the project root:
  > python .claude\skills\project_map\map_watcher.py
- On first run, it asks what type of project structure you have:
  1. Split (separate FE + BE)
  2. Unified (Blazor Server, MVC, monolith)
- The watcher generates an initial map immediately.
- Subsequent updates occur every 60 seconds.
- Configuration is saved to `watcher_config.json` for future runs.

4. Configure Claude Rules
- Create or update `.claude/rules.md` with:
  System: Always consult `.claude/idev/project-map/project.map.md` before making any decisions.

How It Works
------------
1. Watcher (`map_watcher.py`) asks for project type on first run.
2. Updater (`ai_map_updater.py`) generates `project.map.md`.
3. Claude reads `project.map.md` for persistent project knowledge.

For Split projects, map includes:
   - Frontend files (.ts, .tsx, .json)
   - Backend files (.cs, .json)
   - Domain entities summary

For Unified projects (Blazor/MVC), map categorizes into:
   - Pages / UI Components (.razor, .cshtml)
   - Services / Interfaces
   - Domain / Entities
   - Infrastructure / Data
   - Other files

4. The watcher never modifies code, only updates the map.

Configuration
-------------
The watcher saves its config to `watcher_config.json`. Example configs:

Split project:
  {
    "project_type": "split",
    "frontend_path": "C:\\path\\to\\frontend",
    "backend_path": "C:\\path\\to\\backend",
    "unified_path": null
  }

Unified project (Blazor Server):
  {
    "project_type": "unified",
    "unified_path": "/path/to/project/src",
    "frontend_path": null,
    "backend_path": null
  }

To reconfigure, run the watcher and answer "n" when asked to use existing config.

Tips
----
- Keep `project.map.md` inside `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/project-map` for consistency.
- Adjust `IGNORE_DIRS` in `ai_map_updater.py` for your project structure.
- Change `UPDATE_INTERVAL` in `map_watcher.py` to adjust update frequency.
